id     = "drag-chip"
about  = """A drag (design.md "Drag and drop": `drag:` on the source): a chip in a bar
row is pressed, dragged 80 px to the right and released; it follows the
pointer while held, lifted out of its row's layout, and springs back to its
slot after the release (there is no target to drop on). The chips either side
of it stay still the whole time."""
screen = { width = 320, scale = 1.0 }

=== shell.strand
bar Top {
  height: 30
  row { id: strip; height: 24; gap: 8; align: center; pad: 0, 8
    box { id: left; width: 30; height: 16; radius: 4; bg: #61afef }
    box { id: chip; width: 30; height: 16; radius: 4; bg: #c678dd; drag: "chip" }
    box { id: right; width: 30; height: 16; radius: 4; bg: #98c379 }
  }
}

=== steps
rest
mark drag
drag 61,15 -> 141,15 over 200
intend #chip moves
rest
expect still #left
expect still #right
mark settled
frames 10
expect still #chip
